# Environment variables — NK Deliveri
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (never committed — see .gitignore) and fill
# in real values for local development. In Vercel, set the same names under
# Project Settings → Environment Variables instead of a file.
#
# Every variable below is grep-verified against actual usage in src/ as of
# this writing (see docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md for the full audit). Two naming
# patterns are used side by side on purpose: `VITE_*` variables are
# inlined into the browser bundle at build time (Vite's own convention —
# never put a real secret in one of these), while the unprefixed variants
# are read via `process.env` server-side only (SSR, server functions).
# Supabase's URL and publishable/anon key are safe in both forms since
# they're designed to be public; the service role key and VAPID private
# key must only ever exist in the unprefixed, server-only form.

# --- Supabase (required) ------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API. The publishable/anon key is safe to
# expose to the browser (it's what RLS exists to protect against); the
# service role key bypasses RLS entirely and must never reach the client.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# Server-only. Used by src/integrations/supabase/client.server.ts for admin
# operations (push notification dispatch, refund/dispute lookups, etc.)
# that must bypass RLS. NEVER prefix this with VITE_ — that would ship it
# to every visitor's browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# --- Web Push notifications (required for push to work) -----------------
# Generate a VAPID key pair once (e.g. `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`)
# and keep it stable — rotating it invalidates every existing push
# subscription. VAPID_PRIVATE_JWK is the private key in JWK JSON form (see
# @block65/webcrypto-web-push's docs for the exact shape); VAPID_SUBJECT is
# a mailto: or https: URL identifying who's sending the push.
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:contact@example.com
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=your-vapid-public-key
VAPID_PRIVATE_JWK={"kty":"EC","crv":"P-256","x":"...","y":"...","d":"..."}

# --- Transactional email (required for the newsletter send feature) -----
# https://resend.com — used by src/lib/send-newsletter.functions.ts.
# Without it, admin bulk newsletter sends fail with a clear error; nothing
# else in the app depends on it.
RESEND_API_KEY=your-resend-api-key

# --- Error monitoring (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Sentry (https://sentry.io). Leave both unset to disable monitoring
# entirely — src/lib/sentry.server.ts and src/lib/sentry-browser.ts both
# no-op with zero overhead when their DSN is absent. Use two *separate*
# Sentry projects (or at least be deliberate about it) since one is
# client-side (browser) and one is server-side (Node) — mixing them makes
# issue triage harder.
SENTRY_DSN=
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# Optional: tags client-side Sentry events with a release identifier.
# Vercel deployments already get this server-side for free via its own
# auto-provided VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA (see docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md) — this is
# only needed if you want the same tagging in the browser bundle.
VITE_COMMIT_SHA=

# --- MonCash payment provider (optional — inactive until fully set) -----
# Secrets for the MonCash disbursement integration
# (src/lib/payment-providers/moncash-provider.server.ts). Server-only —
# never prefix any of these with VITE_. Every value below is read
# exclusively through src/lib/payment-providers/moncash-config.server.ts,
# the single module allowed to touch process.env.MONCASH_*; nothing else
# in the app should read these directly.
#
# Leaving all five unset is safe and is the default in every environment
# today: moncashProvider.isConfigured() reports false, the orchestrating
# server function (initiate-provider-payout.functions.ts) refuses to call
# it, and the admin payout UI already hides this provider from selection
# (payment_providers.moncash_api.is_active = false in the database) until
# it is deliberately activated. Setting all five here does NOT activate
# real transfers by itself — the actual HTTP calls aren't implemented yet
# (see docs/PAYMENT_PROVIDERS.md for why). See that same doc for where to
# obtain each value and the rotation procedure.
MONCASH_CLIENT_ID=
MONCASH_CLIENT_SECRET=
MONCASH_MERCHANT_ID=
MONCASH_API_URL=
MONCASH_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- PLOP payment provider (optional — inactive until fully set) --------
# Secrets for the PLOP Collect integration
# (src/lib/payment-providers/plop-provider.server.ts) — the backend behind
# the "MonCash Automatik" checkout method (payment_provider_settings.
# provider = 'moncash_auto'), replacing the dormant Digicel-direct
# integration above. Server-only — never prefix any of these with VITE_.
# Every value below is read exclusively through
# src/lib/payment-providers/plop-config.server.ts, the single module
# allowed to touch process.env.PLOP_*; nothing else in the app should
# read these directly. See docs/PLOP_PHASE0_AUDIT.md for where each value
# comes from (PLOP merchant portal) and docs/PLOP_PHASE1_ARCHITECTURE.md
# for the full architecture.
#
# Leaving both required values unset is safe and is the default in every
# environment today: plopProvider.isConfigured() reports false, and
# moncash_auto stays enabled=false in payment_provider_settings until
# deliberately activated after real testing (docs/PLOP_PHASE1_ARCHITECTURE.md
# § 7).
PLOP_CLIENT_ID=
PLOP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional — defaults to "moncash" (the only rail this replacement
# covers) if unset. Only change this if PLOP's merchant_id account is
# reconfigured for a different rail (kashpaw/natcash/all).
PLOP_PAYMENT_METHOD=

# Secures src/routes/api.cron.moncash-reconcile.ts AND
# src/routes/api.cron.plop-reconcile.ts (Vercel Cron, see vercel.json's
# `crons` entries) — Vercel automatically sends `Authorization: Bearer
# <this value>` on scheduled invocations once set
# (https://vercel.com/docs/cron-jobs/manage-cron-jobs#securing-cron-jobs).
# Without it, both endpoints always return 500 rather than running
# unauthenticated. Generate any random 32+ byte value (e.g. `openssl rand
# -hex 32`) — it's a shared secret, not tied to either provider.
CRON_SECRET=

# --- Routing (optional) --------------------------------------------------
# Defaults to the public router.project-osrm.org demo server if unset —
# fine for development, but that demo server is rate-limited and
# explicitly not meant for production traffic (see src/services/routing.ts).
# Point this at a self-hosted OSRM instance before real launch.
VITE_OSRM_URL=

# --- Auto-provided by Vercel — do not set manually ------------------------
# VERCEL_ENV, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA (and many more) are injected
# automatically by Vercel's build/runtime environment and consumed by
# src/lib/sentry.server.ts for environment/release tagging. Only relevant
# if you're deliberately reproducing a Vercel-like environment locally
# (e.g. `vercel env pull`) — never define these yourself in .env.local.
